Those unchanged firmware arrays were extracted for testing only. They are
not bundled as our OS implementation.

Wired networking in0.9
With the VM powered off, configure the existing VM without changing disks:
VBoxManage modifyvm "Zero OS" --nic1 nat --nictype1 Am79C973 --cableconnected1 on
Then boot and use net to inspect its connection. No manual connect command
is required. A host connected over WiFi still supplies virtual Ethernet to
the guest; this is not native guest WiFi. Other virtual NIC models have no
driver in this version. QEMU PCnet tests pass; native VirtualBox remains
unverified in this workspace because its host kernel driver is unavailable.
